  "title": "The Power of Attunement",
  "content": "Attunement is the ability to notice, understand, and respond to your child’s emotional state. It is the heart of secure attachment. When a parent is attuned, the child feels seen and understood. This does not require mind‑reading; it simply means paying attention to cues such as tone, posture, facial expressions, and behaviour.\n\nChildren who experience attunement learn that their feelings matter. They become better at recognising and expressing emotions. When attunement is missing, children may feel confused, alone, or overwhelmed. But attunement can be learned and strengthened at any stage of parenting.\n\nThis lesson teaches parents how to slow down, observe, and respond in ways that build emotional connection.",
  "activities": [
    "Watch your child for two minutes today without speaking. Notice their mood, energy, and body language.",
